*.local

# Env files. `.env.local` is already covered by *.local, but a plain `.env`
# was not — one careless `echo KEY=... > .env` would have committed a live
# secret to a PUBLIC repo. Ignore them all, then force-track the two that are
# safe by construction: .env.example holds names only, and VITE_-prefixed
# values are compiled into the client bundle so they can never be secret.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production
.DS_Store
.session

